' diagram-type: c4-container
@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title v0002 State Registry - Team-Scoped C4 Container Architecture

actor "System Admin" as Admin
actor Operator
component Listeners
component Executors
component WebUI
component Gateway
component State
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

Admin --> State : POST /admin/teams, /admin/source-systems,\n/admin/task-types (create-only)\nGET /admin/tags, /admin/tasks (read-only)
Operator --> WebUI
WebUI --> Gateway
Gateway --> State : trusted one-team context
Listeners --> State : submit tasks
Executors --> State : claim with command_id
State --> DB : 3NF persistence

note right of Executors
  Concrete Executor services follow the platform naming convention
  documented in AGENTS.md:
    executor_<runtime>_<tool>
  Current concrete Executor: executor_docker_opehands
  (runtime = docker, tool = openhands; "opehands" is the service
  identifier; the external product spelling "OpenHands" stays
  unchanged). Future K8s executors will follow the same pattern with
  runtime = k8s and tool selection pending.
end note

note right of State
  Admin /admin/* POST creates teams, source systems, task types
  (team resource is create-only: no PUT/PATCH/DELETE team API).
  GET /admin/tags projects task_types.execution_tag globally;
  GET /admin/tasks returns global current-state summaries.
  Both GET endpoints are read-only, system-admin-only, non-mutating.
  /v1/tasks ingestion requires task_type_id; the Registry derives
  required_tag from task_types.execution_tag (no listener tag).
  /v1/executors/{id}/claim with command_id does FIFO claim.
  Lifecycle: pending -> created (FIRST created event on claim)
  -> running -> finished|failed. Local AES-256-GCM at rest.
  Non-revealing 404 for foreign identifiers. Equal tags across
  teams grant NO authority.
end note

@enduml